<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gallagher cuts yr shr loss, no div.</title>
<headline>Gallagher cuts yr shr loss, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended February 28</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		64 loss     vs 355 loss</p>
<p>    - attrib		 332 loss     vs 355 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib income	  124.86 loss  vs 7.89 loss</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   14.39	 vs 5.30</p>
<p>    Turnover		  24.18	 vs 0.73</p>
<p>    Exceptional items *   95.12 loss  vs nil</p>
<p>Full name: Gallagher Estate Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>* Exceptional items include goodwill written-off and provision for dimunition of property values.</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said future prospects would be largely influenced by the outcome of the Johnnic casino bid on the adjacent property. If successful, Gallagher would derive an income for three years for the lease of one of its exhibition halls and would derive the benefit of substantial structured parking and improved access to the site.</p>
<p>The company said it was overgeared at present and the board was looking at ways of reducing this. This cinlude a further rights offer during the current year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
